  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-DEC Middle East Appeal 2024 Phase 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam seeks to address the urgent food security and basic needs of communities in Gaza to ensure that the most vulnerable, crisis-affected individuals are supported with life-saving humanitarian assistance through improved food security.  In Gaza, under phase 1 of DEC, Oxfam and local partner will target 1900 of the most vulnerable displaced people living in informal shelters with emergency multi purpose cash assistance and protection services
Oxfam has been present in the OPT since the 1950s, with a country office established in the 1980s. Registered in country, Oxfam operates humanitarian and development interventions in the West Bank and Gaza through 70 staff members across offices in Ramallah, Gaza City, and Jerusalem. Approximately 30 Gaza-based staff are directly involved inimplementing responses with support from a team of 10 staff in Jerusalem and others in Jordan and Egypt to manage coordination. Theresponse in Gaza is led by the Response Lead, Gaza Programme lead and the team in Gaza with full functions (programme, support and management) to coordinate the response. Oxfam&apos;s response is partner led, and Oxfam will work with1 national partner in Gaza for the implementation of this project.

Currently, Oxfam is using the following supply lines:
- Egypt: WASH (latrines, bladders, tanks, handwashing stations, hygiene kits), protection and shelter items; ECHO flight shipments from Oxfam&#x2019;s UK Supply Centre to El Arish airport; Food kits and hygiene items procured in Egypt; MOU with IOM for transportation. Currently, Oxfam is looking for other options beyond IOM to support on both procurement and transportation to Gaza via Karam Shalom.
- Jordan: Food kits, WASH items, hygiene items, dignity items procured in Jordan; International ECHO flight shipments to Amman for other WASH items; coordination with Logistics cluster and JCHO for cargo movement. Currently, Oxfam is looking for other options beyond Logs cluster and JCHO to support on cargo movement to Gaza via Erez and Karam Shalom.
- West Bank: Food and hygiene items: Oxfam is exploring this route in addition to the above options, to support the local Palestinian vendors/market</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM GB</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib has been active in the Occupied Palestinian Territory/Israel (OPT/I) since 1982 and working with Palestinian refugees in Lebanon since the mid 1980s. It has built up a strong network of relationships with local NGOs and counts among its localcounterparts some of the largest and most professional NGOs in various sectors. It has accompanied these NGOs in their development from ad hoc volunteer groups to sizeable professional institutions with national outreach.  At the same time the conceptualisation of the programme has evolved from three country programs in the early 1990s to a program for Palestinians in the Middle East (PME) working withPalestinians in OPT, Israel and Lebanon.

The programme has changed over the years with the establishment of the Palestinian Authority (PA) in the mid-1990s from a focus on support and service provision at a grassroots level and grassroots mobilization, to working towards influencing the establishment of the PA, its lawmaking and supporting building a democratic state # this involved supporting efforts of Palestinian civil society to build the basis for a democratic Palestinian state with room for civil participation, ensuring inclusion of vulnerable groups, refugees and women, and shaping its laws and systems. Oxfam Novib has also supported partners that are working on the provision of humanitarian assistance, response preparedness and conflict transformation. We have also supported partners in the provision of health services, access to quality education and gender justice.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
